^ Kustritz, Anne (June 9, 2016). ""They All Lived Happily Ever After. Obviously.": Realism and Utopia in Game of Thrones-Based Alternate Universe Fairy Tale Fan Fiction". Humanities. 5 (2). MDPI: 7. doi:10.3390/h5020043. Game of Thrones fairy tale AUs perfectly exemplify this principle, as these fan works reconceptualize the HBO show, the books the show is based on, and the fairy tale genre, as well as other fan-specific genre conventions, while the books themselves also draw heavily on numerous layers of fairy tale, alternate history, and fantasy novels, films, and stories as intertexts.', 'Ended', 'HBO', 'Winter is coming.', 8.459, 26538, '2011-04-17', '2019-05-19', 194.3937, 'en', 'Game of Thrones', 'https://www.hbo.com/game-of-thrones', 73, 8, 0, 'Scripted', 'US', '/1XS1oqL89opfnbLl8WnZY1O1uJx.jpg', '/zZqpAXxVSBtxV9qPBcscfXBcL2w.jpg', '2026-04-03T15:40:34Z', '2026-04-03T16:03:35Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('212e97f9-3bfb-49d0-8a5b-f3586f06c585', 'Tom''s Midnight Garden', 30428, 251553, 1989, 'Forced to stay with his aunt and uncle for the summer holidays, Tom Long is lonely and bored, until one night he hears the clock strike 13. He suddenly finds himself transported to a magical Victorian garden of the 1880s and meets a girl.', 'Tom Long, a young boy who is sent to stay with his aunt and uncle in their dull, old house during the summer. One night, when the grandfather clock mysteriously strikes thirteen, Tom discovers that the backyard transforms into a magical, Victorian-era garden. There, he meets Hatty, a lonely girl who becomes his companion in this timeless world. As Tom returns to the garden night after night, he notices that time moves strangely—each visit shows Hatty growing older, from a little girl to a young woman, while Tom remains the same age. Through their friendship, Tom unravels the mystery of the garden and Hatty''s life. In the present, he learns that Hatty is now an elderly woman, Mrs. Bartholomew, the upstairs neighbor, whose dreams connect the past and present. The series beautifully explores themes of time, memory, and the power of imagination.', 'Ended', 'BBC One', '', 6.0, 1, '1989-01-04', '1989-02-08', 0.9666, 'en', 'Tom''s Midnight Garden', '', 6, 1, 0, 'Miniseries', 'GB', '/fCJa3Bz9eOZzk9Epv39RAZG6Pp9.jpg', '/AkoIioePKwDMfFY4ib3n0LAZ9ZA.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:17:52Z', '2026-04-03T17:17:57Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('27badad1-7c00-4147-bc51-c8e96063f79b', 'Dogtanian and the Three Muskehounds', 5341, 74972, 1981, 'France, 17th century, under the reign of Louis XIII. Dogtanian is an impetuous and innocent peasant from Gascony, as well as a skilled swordsman, who travels to Paris with the purpose of making his dream come true: to join the Corps of Muskehounds of the Royal Guard.', 'The story, set in 17th-century France, follows a young Dogtanian (D''Artagnan (ダルタニヤン) in the Japanese version and voiced by Satomi Majima (間嶋 里美) and D''Artacán in the Spanish version) who travels from Béarn to Paris in order to become one of King Louis XIII''s musketeers (they are referred to as musketeers throughout the cartoon and only the title calls them ''Muskehounds''). He quickly befriends three musketeers (Porthos, Athos and Aramis), saving Juliette, a maid-in-waiting for Queen Anne of Austria. A key difference between the English-language dubs of the Dogtanian adaptions and Dumas'' novel is that the names of Athos and Porthos were interchanged, making Athos the extrovert and Porthos the secretive noble of the group.', 'Ended', 'MBS', '', 7.307, 70, '1981-10-09', '1982-03-26', 5.9953, 'es', 'D''Artacán y los tres mosqueperros', 'https://brb.es/en/dartacan-y-los-tres-mosqueperros', 26, 1, 0, 'Miniseries', 'JP,ES', '/rHFBZgPpgHIXFz1jP5xdZlkmPqu.jpg', '/juEqGPmRFYd5iBGS4ID2qOnXPv9.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:18:42Z', '2026-04-03T17:18:48Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('27f7efb1-7114-4e2e-9427-635393a6ddb1', 'Kratts'' Creatures', 933, 71102, 1996, 'Kratts'' Creatures is a children''s television program on PBS. The show was hosted by the Kratt Brothers, Chris and Martin. It also featured Shannon Duff as Allison Baldwin and Ron Rubin as the voice of an animated anthropomorphic dinosaur. The show introduced its viewers to the world of animals. 50 episodes were produced in total. The show ran for only one season on PBS from June 3, 1996 until August 9, 1996. Then after cancellation, aired reruns until June 9, 2000. It also aired reruns on PBS Kids Go! from October 2006 to May 2008. Due to its popularity the show inspired an unofficial spinoff, Zoboomafoo, another show created by the Kratts, which premiered on January 25, 1999.', 'The series follows the wildlife adventures of brothers Chris and Martin Kratt as they travel to various locations around the globe—ranging from the African savanna to the Australian Outback and the North American wilderness—to observe wild animals in their natural habitats. The program''s primary goal is to educate children about zoology, ecology, and animal behavior, while emphasizing wildlife conservation and respect for nature.

While the brothers are out in the field on their "creature adventures," they frequently communicate with their home base, a clubhouse known as the Creature Club. The club is managed by Allison Baldwin (Shannon Duff), a young woman who assists the brothers by looking up additional scientific facts, referencing field guides, and monitoring their global coordinates via her computer. The series also features Ttark (voiced by Ron Rubin), an animated, anthropomorphic dinosaur whose name is "Kratt" spelled backward. Ttark appears in interstitial animated segments to provide additional educational facts, correct common misconceptions about animals, and host multiple-choice "Creature Quizzes" to test the viewers'' knowledge. 

Each episode typically focuses on a specific animal, species group, or biological theme, such as predators, animal camouflage, or the developmental struggles of baby animals. Chris and Martin interact closely with the wildlife, utilizing their contrasting but enthusiastic personalities to demonstrate animal behaviors and explain their ecological significance in an accessible manner. The show blends live-action nature documentary footage with fast-paced editing, comedic moments, and interactive facts to keep the educational content engaging. Through their field explorations, the Kratt brothers encourage their target audience of school-aged children to explore the natural world, appreciate biodiversity, and seek out the animals living in their own backyards.', 'Ended', 'PBS', '', 8.3, 3, '1996-06-03', '1996-08-09', 0.7682, 'en', 'Kratts'' Creatures', '', 50, 1, 0, 'Scripted', 'US,CA', '/6FSDfMgrCH1zYSoFppJ0OZVGpBU.jpg', '/j6sBB0eEiszkPB6V78J1GvjBRgQ.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:11:47Z', '2026-04-03T17:12:07Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('2cb2fe67-cc74-4641-ac37-515651fa5eb8', 'The Animals of Farthing Wood', 188, 74638, 1993, 'The Animals of Farthing Wood is an animated series created by the European Broadcasting Union between 1992 and 1995 and based on the series of books written by Colin Dann. It was produced by Telemagination, based in London, and La Fabrique, based in Montpellier in France, but also aired in other European countries. The first countries to air the series were Germany and the United Kingdom, in January 1993.', 'The television series followed the basic plots of the series of books, although certain elements were changed.
The first series followed the animals of Farthing Wood, who were forced to flee their homes after humans started destroying the wood to build suburban tract houses. Led by Fox, and guided by Toad, the animals left Farthing Wood on a journey to White Deer Park, a nature reserve where they would be protected. The second and third series followed the relationships between the Farthing Wood animals, the White Deer Park animals and outsiders, particularly a blue fox named Scarface, his mate Lady Blue and cub Ranger.
The episodes were made in both the UK and France. Because of this, in Series 1 traffic is seen driving on the right hand carriageway of the motorway, but they are briefly seen in Series 3 driving on the left hand side. Other than this, the location is generally kept ambiguous, apart from a brief moment in Series 2 when a gravestone is visible with French writing on it.
When the series aired in the United States, two versions were shown: the UK version which was shown on select television stations, and a new version released on home video titled Journey Home: The Animals of Farthing Wood. The home video version saw some of the voices changed, for example, the role of Fox was replaced by Ralph Macchio, along with added songs as well.

^ FieldmasterFox (25 September 2016), Journey Home The Animal of Fathing Wood Starring Ralph Macchio, retrieved 16 March 2018', 'Ended', 'BBC One', '', 8.245, 55, '1993-01-03', '1995-12-21', 3.3155, 'en', 'The Animals of Farthing Wood', '', 39, 3, 0, 'Scripted', 'GB', '/aRKM4v1j46jxtHR3wfbNTUrYg0T.jpg', '/u8hU5zQ16Mg0qNwp0FgolTVo99H.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:18:48Z', '2026-04-03T17:18:54Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('3259eba1-e2ef-46db-a2bb-f293688c2024', 'Zoboomafoo', 4217, 78794, 1999, 'Zoboomafoo is an American children''s television series that aired from January 25, 1999, to April 28, 2001, and is still shown today in syndication depending on the area, and it is regularly shown on PBS Kids Sprout. A total of 65 episodes were aired. A creation of the Kratt Brothers, it features a talking Coquerel''s Sifaka, a type of lemur, named Zoboomafoo, or Zoboo for short, and a collection of repeat animal guests. Every episode begins with the Kratt brothers in "Animal Junction", a peculiar place in which the rules of nature change and wild animals come to visit and play. After January 16, 2004, the show was pulled from its weekday airing on most PBS stations, though some continue to air the show.', 'Every episode of the series begins with zoologist brothers Chris and Martin Kratt arriving at "Animal Junction," a whimsical wildlife outpost where the normal rules of nature do not apply and animals from all over the world come to visit. Upon arriving, the brothers set out specific snacks—typically items like garbanzo beans, sweet potatoes, and mango slices—to summon their friend Zoboomafoo, a wild Coquerel''s sifaka lemur. A live-action lemur leaps into the room, eats the snacks, lets out a loud burp, and spins around, magically transforming into a talking, energetic lemur puppet. Zoboo, as he is affectionately called, serves as the brothers'' co-host and eager pupil, ready to learn about the day''s animal guests.

The episodes generally revolve around a specific zoological theme, such as baby animals, hibernation, animal families, or locomotion. Early in the episode, Zoboo introduces a "Mystery Animal," providing the Kratts and the viewing audience with a set of clues about a creature he encountered on his way to Animal Junction, whose true identity is revealed later in the broadcast. As the episode progresses, various live animals visit the junction, allowing the brothers to interact with the creatures and educate viewers about their natural habitats, diets, and unique biological adaptations. The program transitions frequently between these live-action studio segments and documentary-style field footage of animals in the wild.

A recurring feature in each episode is a claymation storytelling segment set in "Zobooland." Here, Zoboo shares an imaginative adventure from his youth, featuring colorful, fictional creatures such as Gooble, Narchi, and Sensit, whose behaviors or physical traits often relate back to the episode''s educational theme. The series also incorporates segments focusing on human interactions with wildlife; the Kratts frequently receive letters from children delivered by various bird species, such as a macaw, an owl, or a Harris''s hawk. The brothers answer the children''s questions and introduce video clips of young people assisting, rescuing, and observing animals in their own neighborhoods. 

At the conclusion of the episode, the visiting animals depart Animal Junction. The Kratt brothers and Zoboomafoo reflect on the day''s lessons and sing a recurring goodbye song. Afterward, Zoboomafoo spins around and transforms back into a live-action lemur, leaping out the window to return to his home in Madagascar, while Chris and Martin leave Animal Junction to head out on their next creature adventure.', 'Ended', 'TVOntario', '', 6.7, 33, '1999-01-25', '2001-06-07', 7.2549, 'en', 'Zoboomafoo', 'http://www.pbs.org/zoboo', 65, 2, 0, 'Scripted', 'CA,US', '/5JMgrHBaspcU9KIfC7nTfPFNL9x.jpg', '/OMZrF60GxJa1iUA78SwwRDjd0k.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:10:54Z', '2026-04-03T17:11:20Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('3610e7f0-95b0-4bb5-bf72-cacd6914d36e', 'Ivor the Engine', 2618, 435497, 1976, 'Ivor the Engine is a British children''s animation by Oliver Postgate and Peter Firmin''s Smallfilms company. It is a children''s television series relating the adventures of a small green locomotive who lived in the "top left-hand corner of Wales" and worked for The Merioneth and Llantisilly Railway Traction Company Limited. His friends included Jones the Steam, Evans the Song and Dai Station, among many other characters.', 'The series follows the gentle adventures of Ivor, a small green steam locomotive who lives and works in the "top left-hand corner of Wales." Operating on the rural, single-track Merioneth and Llantisilly Railway Traction Company Limited, Ivor is not merely a machine but a sentient, deeply emotional character with a mind of his own. Unlike typical train engines, Ivor harbors unusual, decidedly human ambitions, such as wishing to sing in a local choir, bathe in a hot spring, or care for a flock of sheep. He is operated by Jones the Steam, an amiable and deeply understanding engine driver who acts as Ivor''s closest companion. Jones treats Ivor more like a pet or a friend than a vehicle, frequently accommodating the engine''s quirky desires and translating his various "peep-peeps" for the rest of the community.

The railway and its surrounding villages are populated by an eccentric but close-knit community of affectionate Welsh caricatures. The practical operations of the railway are overseen by Dai Station, the strict and perpetually flustered stationmaster at Llaniog. Dai is a stickler for company rules and frequently despairs at Ivor''s unorthodox behavior, though he ultimately harbors a soft spot for the engine. Other prominent local figures include Evans the Song, the passionate choirmaster of the Grumbly and District Choral Society; Mrs. Porty, a wealthy, eccentric aristocratic woman; and Mr. Dinwiddy, a highly unconventional gold miner who lives up in the hills and spends his time inventing bizarre contraptions. A central and iconic character introduced during the series is Idris, a small, red, fire-breathing Welsh dragon. Hatched from a mysterious egg discovered on the railway lines, Idris takes up permanent residence inside Ivor''s firebox to keep warm and eventually joins the choir. 

Episodes typically revolve around the low-stakes, slice-of-life happenings of the village and Ivor''s daily routines, employing a comforting, storybook atmosphere. Rather than focusing on high drama or fast-paced action, the narratives celebrate community cooperation, gentle eccentricity, and problem-solving. A major recurring narrative and stylistic element is music; Ivor communicates and expresses his emotions through a trio of resonant notes mimicking his steam whistle, an effect famously achieved using a bassoon. This inherent musicality drives much of the overarching plot, most notably when Ivor achieves his dream of becoming the bass voice in the local choral society. Presented through charmingly rudimentary cardboard cut-out animation, the entire series is unified by the soothing storytelling of Oliver Postgate, who provided the narration and voiced all the characters, lending the program a distinctive, whimsical charm.', 'Ended', 'ITV1', '', 7.0, 3, '1976-01-26', '1977-12-23', 1.5788, 'en', 'Ivor the Engine', '', 97, 5, 0, 'Scripted', 'GB', '/79VQwrUHwmIhh50BlvUV3aqh0mb.jpg', '/8jBafwkUk3pIh8Sj1JV5LPc4hJA.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:24:24Z', '2026-04-03T17:24:51Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('38224aab-22fe-4b2d-b015-2e17038fde3b', 'Madeline', 17194, 101611, 1988, 'A young girl embarks on a series of misadventures, causing her friends and teachers to be worrisome. Based on the children''s books by Ludwig Bemelmans.', 'The series is set in Paris, France, and revolves around the daily lives and adventures of twelve young girls attending a Catholic boarding school. The girls live in an "old house in Paris that was covered with vines" and are cared for and taught by Miss Clavel, a strict but deeply affectionate nun. The show focuses heavily on the titular Madeline, who is the smallest of the twelve girls but also the most fearless and adventurous. Despite her good intentions, Madeline''s curiosity and bold nature frequently lead her and her classmates into various misadventures, ranging from exploring the city and getting lost, to rescuing animals and helping those in need. 

A recurring element in the series is Miss Clavel''s keen maternal intuition; whenever Madeline or the other girls find themselves in trouble, Miss Clavel often suddenly awakens or stops her activities, declaring, "Something is not right!" before rushing to their aid. The girls are frequently joined in their escapades by Pepito, the son of the Spanish Ambassador who lives next door. Originally introduced in the source material as a mischievous "bad hat" who plays cruel pranks, the series depicts Pepito as a reformed, loyal friend who shares in Madeline''s adventures. Other prominent characters include Genevieve, a highly intelligent stray dog who saves Madeline from drowning and becomes the school''s beloved pet, and Lord Covington, the cantankerous head of the school''s board of trustees whom Madeline secretly but affectionately nicknames "Cuckoo Face."

Episodes typically follow the group as they navigate everyday problems, explore famous landmarks around Paris or other international locales, and learn valuable moral lessons about honesty, teamwork, courage, and compassion. To honor the children''s books by Ludwig Bemelmans upon which the show is based, the series utilizes a narrator who often speaks in rhyming couplets to drive the story forward. Every episode begins with the classic opening lines from the original 1939 book, establishing the comforting, storybook tone of the series, and concludes with Miss Clavel turning out the bedroom light and the narrator stating, "That''s all there is; there isn''t any more."', 'Ended', 'ABC', '', 5.7, 34, '1988-11-07', '2001-02-28', 8.873, 'en', 'Madeline', '', 65, 3, 0, 'Scripted', 'US,FR,CA', '/kh1xdNqCYj4plWOyYjSIrPzzUvI.jpg', '/kNTaLz6t7JTaRyWZXpriBg6asGn.jpg', '2026-04-03T16:34:01Z', '2026-04-03T16:52:01Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('3f51cdd3-08df-42f8-806f-78d3958c3166', 'The Witcher', 71912, 362696, 2019, 'Geralt of Rivia, a mutated monster-hunter for hire, journeys toward his destiny in a turbulent world where people often prove more wicked than beasts.', 'The story begins with Geralt of Rivia, Crown Princess Cirilla of Cintra, and the quarter-elf sorceress Yennefer of Vengerberg at different points in time, exploring formative events that shape their characters throughout the first season, before eventually merging into a single timeline.
Geralt and Ciri are linked by destiny since before she was born when he unknowingly demanded her as a reward for his services by invoking "the Law of Surprise". After the two finally meet, Geralt becomes the princess''s protector and must help her and fight against her various pursuers to prevent her Elder Blood and powerful magic from being used for malevolent purposes and keep Ciri and their world safe.', 'Returning Series', 'Netflix', 'Destiny is a beast.', 7.935, 6608, '2019-12-20', '2025-10-30', 60.1672, 'en', 'The Witcher', 'https://www.netflix.com/title/80189685', 32, 4, 1, 'Scripted', 'US', '/AoGsDM02UVt0npBA8OvpDcZbaMi.jpg', '/foGkPxpw9h8zln81j63mix5B7m8.jpg', '2026-04-03T15:40:44Z', '2026-04-03T16:03:47Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('4363c674-ad55-4e79-99dc-101bee2108c9', 'The Real Housewives of D.C.', 31493, 170151, 2010, 'The Real Housewives of D.C. is an American reality television series that debuted August 5, 2010, on Bravo. It is the network''s fifth installment in The Real Housewives series. On April 7, 2011, Bravo announced that The Real Housewives of D.C. had been cancelled. This was a first in the history of the franchise that one of its series had not been renewed.', 'In its series premiere, The Real Housewives of D.C. introduced Mary Amons, Lynda Erkiletian, Cat Ommanney, Michaele Salahi, and Stacie Scott Turner, focusing on their personal and professional lives within the political and social circles of Washington, D.C. Early storylines established the women''s prominent social standings and immediate personality clashes. Amons, a wealthy socialite and granddaughter of television personality Arthur Godfrey, attempted to serve as the neutral peacemaker of the group while managing her large family and philanthropic endeavors. Erkiletian, the owner of a prominent modeling agency, navigated the societal judgments surrounding her relationship with her significantly younger boyfriend, Ebong. Meanwhile, Turner, a successful real estate agent, embarked on a deeply emotional personal journey to locate her biological father and connect with her extended family. 

Ommanney, a blunt British interior designer working on a memoir about her life and past relationships, frequently ignited conflict within the group due to her unfiltered opinions. Her outspoken political views and criticisms of then-President Barack Obama caused significant friction, particularly with Turner. Simultaneously, suspicion began to mount among the women regarding Salahi and her husband, Tareq. Erkiletian openly questioned Salahi''s health and erratic behavior, suggesting she might be suffering from an eating disorder—a claim Salahi vehemently denied, later revealing she had been diagnosed with multiple sclerosis. The Salahis consistently boasted about their wealth, elite political connections, and involvement in high-profile polo matches, though the other women grew increasingly skeptical of their grandiose claims and apparent financial instability. 

The season''s narrative was ultimately dominated by a highly publicized real-life scandal when Michaele and Tareq Salahi famously breached Secret Service security to attend a White House state dinner uninvited. The series captured the couple preparing for the event honoring Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh, as well as the immediate and severe fallout that ensued. The unprecedented security breach launched a federal investigation, became a massive national news story, and brought intense media and government scrutiny to the Bravo production. The incident completely shattered any remaining trust between Salahi and the rest of the cast, who rapidly distanced themselves from the couple out of fear for their own reputations and careers. In the subsequent reunion special, the women aggressively confronted Salahi over the state dinner incident, her documented history of fabrications, and the couple''s overall deceit. Due to the intense controversy and the unbridgeable divide among the cast, the series was put on an indefinite hiatus and subsequently canceled, marking the first time a Real Housewives installment was not renewed for a second season.', 'Ended', 'Bravo', 'I don''t make money, I spend money.', 4.0, 5, '2010-08-05', '2010-10-21', 0.6373, 'en', 'The Real Housewives of D.C.', 'http://www.bravotv.com/the-real-housewives-of-dc', 11, 1, 0, 'Reality', 'US', '/uXkmzijKgBYAkeXas453ZrQxnNg.jpg', '/1FugcefO6h1jE6i85iTx61cPa8l.jpg', '2026-04-03T16:35:01Z', '2026-04-03T16:53:54Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('43ec5857-0a06-4270-abe7-9084053c1a19', 'The Borrowers', 40306, 81205, 1992, 'The Borrowers are small, 15cm high humans who live in the English hinterland. They live out their lives in mouse-hole sized nooks in human homes, and survive by ''borrowing'' all they need from the house and its inhabitants. This series follows young girl Arriety, and her parents Pod and Homily, as they are displaced from their home and try to find a new home, with the help of a human boy, George.', 'The Clock Family are "borrowers," tiny people who live in the houses of regular sized "human beans" (a borrower mispronunciation of human beings). They survive by borrowing all they need from big people and try to keep their existence secret. The main characters are a teenage borrower girl named Arrietty and her parents, Pod and Homily. During a borrowing expedition with her father and contrary to borrower nature, Arrietty befriends a human boy named George who lives in the home and develops a friendship with him.
The tiny family, who live under the kitchen floorboards of an old manor (Chawton House in Hampshire was used for on location filming), are eventually discovered by the other humans who occupy the home and are forced to flee into the English countryside. After finding an old boot to live in, the family befriends a fellow Borrower – a young man who goes by the name "Dreadful Spiller". Spiller helps them find a more permanent home by reuniting them with relations who had formerly run away from the same manor after one of them was seen and eventually relocated in the caretaker''s cabin on the manor''s grounds.', 'Ended', 'BBC Two', '', 6.4, 11, '1992-11-08', '1993-12-19', 3.436, 'en', 'The Borrowers', '', 12, 2, 0, 'Miniseries', 'GB', '/sZaefhd3UeSeEso2rCcIPAewjDu.jpg', '/eK20eVn1JfJqUIYnrmdJfR8agHi.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:17:46Z', '2026-04-03T17:17:52Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('4a6f36ef-8e46-4297-b58f-def3c13e83a2', 'Bear in the Big Blue House', 207, 70622, 1997, 'The series provides children with valuable tools for growth in key areas of music, social skill development, and cognitive learning through integrated programs combining music, movement, and exploration. With Bear and all his friends, learn about cooperation, teamwork and more.', 'Bear lives in the Big Blue House where he is a caregiver for his friends Ojo, a bear cub, Tutter, a mouse, Treelo, a lemur, otters Pip and Pop, and storyteller Shadow. He and his friends have many adventures together. Those normally include solving problems, sharing, cooperating with each other, and developing social/life skills.
Each episode opens with the welcome song, Bear detecting a scent in the viewers (which he likens to a pleasant smell) and appearance of the characters. Every episode focuses on an individual theme (e.g. sleep, doctors, and Thanksgiving) which folds into a lesson at the end. Songs and jokes accompany the episode. Most episodes feature the character Shadow narrating a segment with shadow puppets. Most of the segments are in song, while some are simply a short story relating to the episode''s theme. At the end of the program, Bear sings the goodbye song with Luna, the moon.', 'Ended', 'Playhouse Disney', '', 7.5, 106, '1997-10-20', '2010-01-01', 12.9352, 'en', 'Bear in the Big Blue House', 'http://www2.disney.co.uk/DisneyChannel/playhouse/friends/bear/index.htm', 117, 4, 0, 'Scripted', 'US', '/hww73tErgeSOQ6YlcKjey0smc8s.jpg', '/sJzekWt8wobtQZel7n8gM3NjiVt.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:35:31Z', '2026-04-03T17:35:37Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('4c7f47af-e049-449d-91cd-73923f2f9ac4', 'Ghostwriter', 3925, 72889, 1992, 'Ghostwriter is an American television program created by Liz Nealon and produced by the Children''s Television Workshop and BBC One. It began airing on PBS on October 4, 1992, and the final episode aired on February 13, 1995. The series revolves around a close knit circle of friends from Brooklyn who solve neighborhood crimes and mysteries as a team of young detectives with the help of an invisible ghost named Ghostwriter. Ghostwriter can communicate with the kids only by manipulating whatever text and letters he can find and using them to form words and sentences. The series was filmed on location in Fort Greene, Brooklyn.', 'The series is designed to teach reading, writing, and critical thinking skills to schoolchildren. Each mystery is presented as a case, covering four 30-minute episodes (except for the first and fifth story arc, where there are five 30 minute episodes); children are encouraged to follow each mystery and use the reading and writing clues given to attempt to solve them just as the Ghostwriter team does. Supervising producer Miranda Barry recalled arguing strongly for filming the series on location in the real setting of Fort Greene, Brooklyn, and noted that there was a year long gap between the pilot and the filming of the rest of the episodes.

^ Bernstein, Sharon (May 17, 1991). "Public TV: ''Ghostwriter'' targets third- and fourth-graders, 40% of whom are said to lack basic reading skills. The series will debut in 1992". Los Angeles Times. Archived from the original on November 7, 2012. Retrieved August 27, 2010.

^ Grundhauser, Eric (February 19, 2016). "Everything You''ve Ever Wanted To Know About ''Ghostwriter''". Atlas Obscura. Retrieved March 16, 2025.', 'Canceled', 'BBC Two', '', 7.0, 14, '1992-10-03', '1995-02-12', 9.483, 'en', 'Ghostwriter', '', 87, 4, 0, 'Scripted', 'US,GB', '/1enj0PMkMBUtRYbWZbfsmv7DUrO.jpg', '/pRKydsDEs69Sp6rFHEKgLhoT2TJ.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:40:27Z', '2026-04-03T17:40:34Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('50bd2746-4b5c-4732-8f78-ab2e87b4d161', 'Liberty''s Kids', 11110, 77619, 2002, 'Liberty''s Kids is an animated educational historical fiction television series produced by DIC Entertainment, originally broadcast on PBS Kids from September 2, 2002 to April 4, 2003, although PBS continued to air reruns until August 2004. The show has since been syndicated by DiC to affiliates of smaller television networks such as The CW and MyNetworkTV and some independent stations so that those stations can fulfill FCC educational and informational requirements. Since September 16, 2006, the series aired on CBS''s new block called KOL Secret Slumber Party on CBS, then it was aired on KEWLopolis, which taking September 12, 2009. In 2008 it ran on The History Channel. The series is currently on the Cookie Jar Toons block on This TV and CBS''s Cookie Jar TV. In 2012, Qubo announced the channel will air Liberty''s Kids in fall 2012. The series was based on an idea by Kevin O''Donnell and developed for television by Kevin O''Donnell, Robby London, Mike Maliani, and Andy Heyward.', 'Benjamin Franklin and four fictional associates experience the American Revolution. Although the series spans 16 years from the Boston Tea Party in 1773 to the ratification of the U.S. Constitution and George Washington becoming the first U.S. president in 1789, no main characters appear to age much, except for Dr. Franklin.', 'Ended', 'PBS', '', 7.6, 19, '2002-09-02', '2003-04-04', 5.8919, 'en', 'Liberty''s Kids', '', 40, 1, 0, 'Scripted', 'US', '/uAJYUum6922FcIlLiOLbJGRqQTP.jpg', '/6OrFwNfXb8pSdnW14Wm16zWUXGW.jpg', '2026-04-03T17:38:28Z', '2026-04-03T17:38:33Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('542c4382-83d4-4d54-ab69-eda231823f2b', 'The Real Housewives of Potomac', 65300, 303252, 2016, 'Just up the river from our nation’s capital lies a hidden gem—Potomac, Maryland. Its rolling hills, gated mansions, sophisticated prep schools, and exclusive country clubs all serve to keep the area invitation-only. Sprinkled throughout this community are a handful of old-line, wealthy African-American families who have historically broken racial barriers to provide a life of privilege for their children. In a town where entry is granted only through class, pedigree, and lineage, how far will the ladies go to secure their spot at the top of this prestigious circle?', '*The Real Housewives of Potomac* premiered on January 17, 2016, originally developed as a show highlighting the exclusive Jack and Jill organizations before being integrated into the *Real Housewives* franchise. The first season introduced an ensemble consisting of Gizelle Bryant, Ashley Darby, Robyn Dixon, Karen Huger, Charrisse Jackson-Jordan, and Katie Rost. Early storylines focused heavily on the women''s elite social standing, Huger''s strict adherence to traditional Potomac etiquette, Rost''s intense pressure on her boyfriend to propose, and Dixon''s unconventional financial and living arrangement with her ex-husband, former NBA player Juan Dixon. The older women''s skepticism of the younger Darby and her much older Australian husband, Michael, also served as a central conflict. Following Rost''s departure, the second season added Monique Samuels, documenting Jackson-Jordan''s painful divorce and Darby''s struggling restaurant venture. The third season introduced Candiace Dillard and saw Jackson-Jordan demoted to a "friend of" capacity. The season''s narrative was largely dominated by Huger''s highly scrutinized financial woes after her husband''s massive IRS debt was revealed, climaxing in a bizarre, cast-only "press conference" organized by Huger. 

The fourth season heavily centered on serious legal allegations against Michael Darby, who was accused of sexually assaulting a production crew member, prompting intense scrutiny and outrage from the rest of the women before the charges were eventually dropped. The season also highlighted Dillard''s combative relationship with her overbearing mother leading up to her lavish wedding. The fifth season introduced Dr. Wendy Osefo and was completely defined by one of the franchise''s most infamous and explosive moments: a violent physical altercation between Samuels and Dillard at a local winery. The altercation fundamentally fractured the group, leading to Samuels being largely ostracized by the cast, with the exception of Darby and Huger. The tension climaxed at the season five reunion, where Samuels produced a meticulously color-coded "receipts" binder to aggressively expose rumors regarding Bryant''s reconciliation with her ex-husband, megachurch pastor Jamal Bryant. Following the reunion, Samuels departed the series.

The sixth season introduced Mia Thornton and heavily chronicled Osefo''s massive physical and personality transformation, which sparked a bitter feud with Bryant following Bryant''s decision to bring up infidelity rumors regarding Osefo''s husband. The season''s reunion special made franchise history by featuring rapper Nicki Minaj as a surprise guest host who aggressively interrogated the cast. The seventh season featured Jackson-Jordan''s return in a "friend" capacity and plunged the cast into deep toxicity when Bryant accused Dillard''s husband, Chris Bassett, of making her uncomfortable in a private hotel room. The accusation triggered a vicious, season-long war between Bryant and Dillard. Simultaneously, Thornton and Osefo engaged in a highly publicized feud that escalated into a physical clash in Miami involving a thrown drink and purse. Meanwhile, Dixon secretly married Juan but sparked massive fan and network backlash by intentionally hiding his alleged infidelities from the cameras, opting instead to reveal the truth behind a paywall after filming wrapped.

The eighth season introduced attorney Nneka Ihim, while the existing cast became deeply divided into two opposing factions that frequently refused to engage with one another. Storylines centered on Thornton''s shocking separation from her husband Gordon amidst severe financial ruin, Darby''s sluggish and heavily scrutinized divorce proceedings, and a bitter cultural feud between Osefo and Ihim concerning allegations of Nigerian witchcraft and shrine submissions. Due to the completely fractured, increasingly toxic dynamics of the group, Bravo initiated a major cast shakeup following the eighth season, resulting in the departures of both Dillard and franchise veteran Dixon. The ninth season introduced former news anchor Stacey Rusch and sports manager Keiarna Stewart to the main cast. The narrative of the revamped season focused heavily on shifting alliances, Thornton''s controversial new romantic relationship with radio personality Inc, and Huger navigating the severe legal and social ramifications of a highly publicized arrest for a DUI and hit-and-run.', 'Returning Series', 'Bravo', 'The word on the street is that I’m the word on the street.', 5.8, 46, '2016-01-17', '2026-03-01', 7.2955, 'en', 'The Real Housewives of Potomac', 'http://www.bravotv.com/the-real-housewives-of-potomac', 193, 10, 1, 'Reality', 'US', '/lgSkHpr6LXxsh2YXiBrDZHn5wUR.jpg', '/dlVTyTBEkZ9z60dREnN7KngX1gt.jpg', '2026-04-03T16:35:37Z', '2026-04-03T16:56:57Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('55596f06-1a13-4da5-91df-218b92fca64a', 'The Real Housewives of Beverly Hills', 32390, 196741, 2010, 'A reality series that follows some of the most affluent women in the country as they enjoy the lavish lifestyle that only Beverly Hills can provide.', 'The series focuses on the personal and professional lives of a group of affluent women residing in Beverly Hills, California. The early seasons introduced the original ensemble cast: sisters and former child actresses Kyle and Kim Richards, British restaurateur Lisa Vanderpump, philanthropist Adrienne Maloof, Camille Grammer, and Taylor Armstrong. Initial storylines heavily featured the lavish lifestyles and immense wealth of the women, while exposing deep personal fractures beneath the surface. Major ongoing narratives included the intense sibling rivalry and co-dependency between Kyle and Kim, compounded by Kim''s ongoing struggles with alcoholism. The series also captured highly publicized real-life tragedies and scandals, most notably Camille''s bitter divorce from actor Kelsey Grammer in the first season, and Taylor''s concealment of severe domestic abuse, which culminated in the suicide of her husband, Russell Armstrong, prior to the premiere of the second season.

As the series progressed into its middle seasons, the cast underwent significant changes, introducing prominent figures such as Brandi Glanville, Yolanda Hadid, Lisa Rinna, Eileen Davidson, and Erika Girardi. The interpersonal dynamics frequently shifted into intense group conflicts, often ignited by Rinna''s outspoken nature. A central conflict emerged during the sixth season surrounding Yolanda''s battle with Lyme disease, which led to fierce arguments when cast members, prompted by Rinna, discussed rumors that Yolanda was fabricating her symptoms and suffering from Munchausen syndrome. Meanwhile, Kim Richards'' continued battle with addiction led to several relapses, highly erratic behavior, and legal troubles, eventually resulting in her departure from the main cast.

The ninth season marked a major structural shift for the series following a controversy dubbed "Puppygate." The dispute centered on a dog adopted by cast member Dorit Kemsley from Vanderpump''s rescue foundation, which eventually ended up at a kill shelter. The resulting fallout over leaked stories to the press completely shattered the decade-long friendship between Vanderpump and Kyle Richards. Feeling alienated by the entire cast, Vanderpump quit the series before the end of the season and refused to attend the reunion. Following her exit, Kyle assumed the de facto role of the group''s matriarch. The show then welcomed actress Denise Richards and its first Black cast member, Garcelle Beauvais. Denise''s tenure was brief but highly publicized, concluding after the tenth season when she abruptly exited the series amid vehement denials of a rumored sexual affair with Brandi Glanville.

In its later seasons, the series was dominated by severe real-life legal and financial scandals. During the eleventh season, Erika Girardi became the focal point of the show after she filed for divorce from her prominent attorney husband, Tom Girardi. Shortly thereafter, Tom was sued for allegedly embezzling millions of dollars in settlement funds from widows and orphans of plane crash victims to fund the couple''s extravagant lifestyle. Erika''s castmates, particularly newcomer Sutton Stracke, heavily interrogated Erika regarding her knowledge of the crimes, leading to explosive confrontations. The twelfth season saw the introduction of Kyle and Kim''s eldest sister, Kathy Hilton, as a recurring cast member. Although initially popular with fans for her eccentricities, Kathy suffered a meltdown during a cast trip to Aspen. The ensuing off-camera tirade, detailed heavily by Rinna, caused a severe familial rift between Kathy and Kyle, and ultimately led to Rinna''s departure from the franchise.

By the thirteenth season, the narrative focus shifted heavily back to Kyle Richards as her seemingly perfect marriage to real estate broker Mauricio Umansky began to publicly deteriorate. The series documented Kyle''s major lifestyle changes, her intense new friendship with country singer Morgan Wade, and the eventual confirmation of her separation from Umansky after decades of marriage. Alongside Kyle''s marital collapse, the series continued to chronicle the evolving dynamics of the remaining women, including Dorit Kemsley''s struggle with PTSD following a violent home invasion and her own subsequent marital separation, while continually introducing new affluent women into the Beverly Hills social circle.', 'Returning Series', 'Bravo', 'Diamonds under pressure.', 6.4, 102, '2010-10-14', '2026-03-19', 23.5134, 'en', 'The Real Housewives of Beverly Hills', 'http://www.bravotv.com/the-real-housewives-of-beverly-hills', 328, 15, 1, 'Reality', 'US', '/8ktaCSlCgGDMFzgdYc1LYF6CiWq.jpg', '/xmCue1RQDs1BfrHrJwmCD2ETeEb.jpg', '2026-04-03T16:34:53Z', '2026-04-03T16:53:32Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_shows (id, title, tmdb_id, tvdb_id, year, overview, plot, status, network, tagline, vote_average, vote_count, first_air_date, last_air_date, popularity, original_language, original_name, homepage, number_of_episodes, number_of_seasons, in_production, type, origin_country, poster_key, backdrop_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('5648cd2a-194d-4ab9-a2ae-b2f9743f463c', 'Avatar: The Last Airbender', 246, 74852, 2005, 'In a war-torn world of elemental magic, a young boy reawakens to undertake a dangerous mystic quest to fulfill his destiny as the Avatar, and bring peace to the world.', '"Fire Nation" redirects here. For the Native American tribe, see Mascouten.See also: World of Avatar: The Last AirbenderA map of the four nations
Avatar: The Last Airbender is set in a world where human civilization consists of four nations, named after the four classical elements: the Water Tribe, the Earth Kingdom, the Fire Nation, and the Air Nomads. In each nation, certain people, known as "benders" (waterbenders, earthbenders, firebenders, and airbenders), have the ability to telekinetically manipulate and control the element corresponding to their nation, using gestures based on Chinese martial arts. The "Avatar" is the only individual with the ability to bend all four elements.
The Avatar is an international arbiter whose duty is to maintain harmony among the four nations, and act as a mediator between humans and spirits. When the Avatar dies, their spirit is reincarnated in a new body, who will be born to parents in the next nation in a set order known as the Avatar cycle: Fire, Air, Water, and Earth. By tradition, the new Avatar will travel the world to learn all four bending arts, after which they will begin in earnest their role as global peacekeeper. The Avatar can enter a condition known as the "Avatar State", in which they temporarily gain the skills and knowledge of all their past incarnations. Although this is when they are at their most powerful, if the Avatar were ever killed while in the Avatar State, the reincarnation cycle would be broken and the Avatar would cease to exist.

A century ago, young Avatar Aang, afraid of his new responsibilities, fled from his home and was forced into the ocean by a storm. He encased himself and his sky bison Appa in suspended animation in an iceberg near the South Pole. Shortly afterward, Fire Lord Sozin, the ruler of the Fire Nation, launched a world war to expand his nation''s empire. Knowing that the Avatar must be an Air Nomad, he and his army carried out a genocide against the Air Nomads, which he timed with the arrival of a comet that gives firebenders tremendous power. A hundred years later, siblings Katara and Sokka, teenagers of the Southern Water Tribe, accidentally discover Aang and revive him.
In the first season, Aang travels with Katara and Sokka to the Northern Water Tribe to learn waterbending and be prepared to defeat the Fire Nation. Prince Zuko, the banished son of Fire Lord Ozai, pursues them, accompanied by his uncle Iroh, hoping to capture the Avatar in order to restore his honor. Aang is also pursued by Zhao, a Fire Nation admiral aspiring to win Ozai''s favor. When his navy attacks the Northern Water Tribe, Zhao kills the moon spirit; Yue, the princess of the tribe, sacrifices her life to revive it, and Aang drives off the enemy fleet.
In the second season, Aang learns earthbending from Toph Beifong, a blind earthbending prodigy. Zuko and Iroh become refugees in the Earth Kingdom, eventually settling in its capital Ba Sing Se. Aang''s group travels to Ba Sing Se to seek the Earth King''s support for an attack on the Fire Nation during an upcoming solar eclipse, during which firebenders will be powerless. Both groups are pursued by Azula, Zuko''s younger sister. Azula infiltrates Ba Sing Se and instigates a coup d''état against the Earth King, bringing the capital under Fire Nation control. Zuko betrays Iroh and returns to the Fire Nation.
In the third season, Aang and his allies invade the Fire Nation during the eclipse, but are forced to retreat. Zuko abandons the Fire Nation to teach Aang firebending. Aang, raised to respect all life, wrestles with the possibility that he will have to kill Ozai to end the war. When Sozin''s comet returns, Aang confronts Ozai and uses his Avatar powers to strip Ozai of his firebending ability; meanwhile, Aang''s friends liberate Ba Sing Se, destroy the Fire Nation airship fleet, and capture Azula. Zuko is crowned the new Fire Lord and the war comes to an end.

For a more comprehensive list, see List of Avatar: The Last Airbender episodes.
See also: Sozin''s Comet
The series consists of sixty-one episodes. The first episode—an-hour-long premiere—aired on February 21, 2005, on Nickelodeon. The series concluded with a two-hour television movie broadcast on July 19, 2008. Each season of the series is known as a "book", in which each episode is referred to as a "chapter". Each book takes its name from one of the elements Aang must master: Water, Earth, and Fire. The show''s first two seasons each consists of twenty episodes and the third season twenty-one. The entire series has been released on DVD in regions 1, 2, and 4.
As of May 2020, the complete series is available on Netflix in the United States. It became the most popular show on U.S. Netflix within the first week of its release there, despite not being featured on the main page. The show broke the record for longest consecutive appearance on Netflix''s daily top ten list, with 60 straight days on the list, one of only two shows in the top ten record holders that was not a Netflix original series as of July 2020. Later in June 2020, the complete series became available on Paramount+ (at the time CBS All Access) and later on Amazon Prime Video in January 2021.

