Sponsors: F, Z, 19', '1990-12-24', NULL, NULL, '2026-04-03T17:36:38Z', '2026-04-03T17:36:38Z');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO tv_episodes (id, tv_season_id, episode_number, title, overview, air_date, runtime, still_key, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('a9c3942c-3051-416f-9c01-02c54e023a55', '0e419615-4c96-4dde-8ed2-715770ba77bb', 25, 'Let It Go', 'When Bear visits the kitchen for a glass of water, he finds Pip and Pop wanting one as well. They make a dash with the water for the Otter Pond, saying that they have a "serious situation." They tell Bear that they''re worried the Otter Pond is going to dry out and Woodland Valley will turn into a desert. Bear offers them reassurance and then seeks to find out the origin of this rumor. It turns out to have come from a rather surprising source. Later, when rain finally does come in the form of a storm, both Bear and Shadow do their best to assuage the kids'' worries. 

Songs 

Come on In 

You Got to Let It Go 

Shadow Is Here 

No Harm (Alternate Version)', NULL, 25, NULL, '2026-04-03T17:35:32Z', '2026-04-03T17:35:32Z');
